@startuml 07_change4_observer_sequence
title Change4 - creating a booking: publish, notify, queue the e-mail (code after Change4)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E1BEE7
  ParticipantBorderColor Black
  ArrowColor Black
  LifeLineBorderColor Black
}

actor Customer
participant BookingController #FFFFFF
participant BookingService #FFFFFF
participant IPricingPolicySelector #BBDEFB
participant BookingEventPublisher
participant EmailBookingObserver
participant AuditLogBookingObserver
participant EmailService #FFFFFF
participant EmailBackgroundQueue #FFFFFF

Customer -> BookingController : POST /api/bookings
BookingController -> BookingService : CreateBookingAsync(request)
BookingService -> BookingService : validate, check capacity
BookingService -> IPricingPolicySelector : SelectPolicy(carType, pickup, return)
IPricingPolicySelector --> BookingService : IPricingPolicy
BookingService -> BookingService : CalculatePrice, save booking

BookingService -> BookingService : PublishBookingEventAsync(CREATED, header)
BookingService -> BookingEventPublisher : PublishAsync(BookingEvent)

BookingEventPublisher -> EmailBookingObserver : OnBookingEventAsync(event)
EmailBookingObserver -> EmailService : SendEmailAsync(to, subject, body)
EmailService -> EmailBackgroundQueue : Enqueue(work item)
EmailService --> EmailBookingObserver
EmailBookingObserver --> BookingEventPublisher

BookingEventPublisher -> AuditLogBookingObserver : OnBookingEventAsync(event)
AuditLogBookingObserver -> AuditLogBookingObserver : LogInformation("Booking audit: ...")
AuditLogBookingObserver --> BookingEventPublisher

BookingEventPublisher --> BookingService
BookingService --> BookingController : BookingResponseDTO
BookingController --> Customer : 200 OK

note over BookingEventPublisher
  An observer that throws is logged as a warning and skipped;
  the next observer still runs and the HTTP result does not change.
end note
note over EmailBackgroundQueue
  EmailQueueHostedService sends the queued
  e-mail later, on a background thread.
end note
@enduml
